lavender: contiguous arena for GPU-shareable IOSurfaces (sweetsurf_arena=MB, 256 with gpu=1)

- SweetSurface: 32 MB contiguous chunks taken at IOCoreSurfaceRoot start; BGRA surfaces with 64-byte rows are
  parts of them (IOSubMemoryDescriptor), so the GPU reads them in place instead of eagl copying them
- idea from the first lavender project (its 1018/1019); made by xnu/src/mk_arena.py

